WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.849
School closed for winter vacation, and when it reopened in February, Davy and Dora were new students in first grade.

2
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:15.547
"I think school is great fun," Davy told Marilla after his first day at school.

3
00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:22.955
"You said I'd find it hard to sit still, and I did . . . but I can wriggle my legs under the desk, and that helps.

4
00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:31.478
"Christopher Cotton drew a picture of Anne on his slate," Davy continued, "and it was really ugly, so I told him I'd hit him at recess.

5
00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:37.955
Christopher said he wasn't scared of me, but he rubbed out Anne's name and put Barbara Shaw's instead."

6
00:00:37.956 --> 00:00:43.006
Marilla frowned. She wasn't pleased that Davy was making threats at school.

7
00:00:43.007 --> 00:00:48.766
"Well, at least he is making friends," she thought a moment later.

8
00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:54.287
One Friday afternoon Diana and Anne met at Green Gables.

9
00:00:54.288 --> 00:01:00.335
They had been invited to tea at Diana's cousin's house in Grafton and had decided to walk.

10
00:01:00.336 --> 00:01:06.364
When they came to a fork in the road, they took the left road when they should have taken the right.

11
00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:12.559
Soon they were lost. "Where are we?" exclaimed Diana.

12
00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.660
"Oh, we must have taken a wrong turn," said Anne.

13
00:01:16.661 --> 00:01:24.160
"We'll never get there by five o'clock—it's half past four now," said Diana with a despairing look at her watch.

14
00:01:24.161 --> 00:01:27.979
"Let's keep going. I think there's a short cut ahead."

15
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:32.040
A few minutes later, the road forked again.

16
00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:36.133
"Which road do we take?" asked Diana anxiously.

17
00:01:36.134 --> 00:01:43.710
Anne shook her head. "I don't know. There's a gate and a lane leading right into the woods.

18
00:01:43.711 --> 00:01:49.184
There must be a house at the end. Let's go there and inquire."

19
00:01:49.185 --> 00:01:53.827
"What a romantic old lane this is," said Diana.

20
00:01:53.828 --> 00:01:58.553
"It's like an enchanted forest," said Anne.

21
00:01:58.554 --> 00:02:02.592
Diana exclaimed, "Oh, I know where we are now.

22
00:02:02.593 --> 00:02:07.239
That is the little stone house where Miss Lavender Lewis lives."

23
00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:14.999
"It's the sweetest, prettiest place I ever saw or imagined," said Anne with delight.

24
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.088
"It looks like something from a storybook."

25
00:02:18.089 --> 00:02:22.198
The house was built of stone and was covered in ivy.

26
00:02:22.199 --> 00:02:31.552
"It will be interesting to meet Miss Lewis ," said Diana as they opened the gate into the garden. "I've heard she is very peculiar."

27
00:02:31.553 --> 00:02:35.185
"She'll be interesting then," said Anne firmly.

28
00:02:35.186 --> 00:02:42.359
"Peculiar people are always interesting at least!" They reached the front door and knocked.

29
00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:50.514
"She used to be engaged to Stephen Irving, Paul's father," Diana said. "But they quarreled and parted."

30
00:02:50.515 --> 00:02:55.318
"Hush," warned Anne. "The door is opening."

31
00:02:55.319 --> 00:03:00.743
A girl of about 14 opened the door and showed them into the parlor.

32
00:03:00.744 --> 00:03:05.278
"Miss Lavender must be expecting company for tea," Anne whispered.

33
00:03:05.279 --> 00:03:09.255
"There are six places set at the table."

34
00:03:09.256 --> 00:03:16.491
Miss Lavender Lewis came in. She was a little lady with light hair and big brown eyes.

35
00:03:16.492 --> 00:03:20.476
"We wanted to ask the right way to Grafton," said Diana.

36
00:03:20.477 --> 00:03:23.629
"We took the wrong path coming through the woods.

37
00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:26.381
Do we go left or right at your gate?"

38
00:03:26.382 --> 00:03:34.300
"Left," said Miss Lavender. Then she exclaimed, "But, oh, won't you stay and have tea with me?

39
00:03:34.301 --> 00:03:41.374
Please do! You'll get to Grafton too late, and Charlotte and I would love for you to stay."

40
00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:47.865
"We'd like to stay," said Anne promptly, for she wanted to get to know Miss Lavender better.

41
00:03:47.866 --> 00:03:52.202
"But you are expecting other guests, aren't you?"

42
00:03:52.203 --> 00:04:00.696
"I know you'll think I'm silly," she said. "I am silly. I'm not expecting anybody. I was just pretending.

43
00:04:00.697 --> 00:04:10.652
You see, I was so lonely and I love company, but few people ever come here because it is so far out of the way. Charlotte was lonely too.

44
00:04:10.653 --> 00:04:17.620
So I baked a cake and got dressed up, but we were just pretending."

45
00:04:17.621 --> 00:04:23.128
Diana secretly thought Miss Lavender was just as peculiar as she had heard.

46
00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:28.270
A woman of 45 pretending to have a tea party, as if she was a little girl!

47
00:04:28.271 --> 00:04:34.668
But Anne exclaimed joyfully, "Oh, do you imagine things too?"

48
00:04:34.669 --> 00:04:38.513
"Yes, I do," Miss Lavender confessed boldly.

49
00:04:38.514 --> 00:04:44.079
"Of course it's silly, but being silly doesn't hurt anybody, and it's fun!

50
00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:47.985
"Now, let's sit down and eat everything!" she went on.

51
00:04:47.986 --> 00:04:50.955
And then they all had a lovely afternoon tea.

52
00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:55.469
As it grew dark, it became time for Anne and Diana to leave.

53
00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:58.745
"You will come again?" Miss Lavender asked.

54
00:04:58.746 --> 00:05:06.424
"Of course!" Anne exclaimed and smiled. She had decided Miss Lavender was a kindred spirit.

55
00:05:06.425 --> 00:05:10.477
As Anne and Diana left, they thanked Miss Lavender.

56
00:05:10.478 --> 00:05:15.922
"Paul Irving would love it here!" Anne said quietly to herself.

57
00:05:15.923 --> 00:05:23.967
"Paul Irving?" Miss Lavender asked. There was a subtle change in her face, and her voice sounded a little different.

58
00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:28.711
"Who is he? I don't know anybody of that name in Avonlea."

59
00:05:28.712 --> 00:05:33.489
Anne was annoyed that she had accidentally mentioned Paul Irving's name.

60
00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:38.291
She had forgotten about Miss Lavender's old romance with Paul's father.

61
00:05:38.292 --> 00:05:41.253
"He is a student of mine," said Anne.

62
00:05:41.254 --> 00:05:45.719
"He moved from Boston to Avonlea this year to live with his grandmother."

63
00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:50.681
"Is he Stephen Irving's son?" Miss Lavender asked.

64
00:05:50.682 --> 00:05:54.250
"Yes, he is," Anne answered.

65
00:05:54.251 --> 00:06:01.514
"Here's some lavender," said Miss Lavender brightly, as if she had not heard the answer to her question.

66
00:06:01.515 --> 00:06:06.261
"Father named me Lavender because he was so fond of it."

67
00:06:06.262 --> 00:06:10.521
Anne and Diana waved good-bye and left.

68
00:06:10.522 --> 00:06:16.031
Diana said, "She seems a little lonely. We must come and visit her."

69
00:06:16.032 --> 00:06:27.790
"Yes!" Anne said. "Her parents named her well—sweet Miss Lavender."

